# Luminary marker — cli#507
- date: 2026-11-08
- branch: fix/507-trust-marker-one-owner
- lead: tony-hoare
- supporting: [john-ousterhout, michael-feathers]
- tony-hoare (lead) — the defect is a missing invariant: "gate ON implies no
  open marker" is stated nowhere and checked nowhere. The fix makes it a
  postcondition of every path that restores the gate.
- john-ousterhout — the marker's lifecycle is split across four functions.
  One consumer, called by both restore paths, is the deep-module shape.
- michael-feathers — the existing tests pass because they build the states by
  hand. The new tests drive the script through real verb sequences instead.
